{"id": "EUVD-2026-108650", "enisaUuid": "67f4ea94-5559-3f50-98d7-d6f4a42ee58f", "description": "`JweRsaKeyEncryptionDecryptorImpl.Decrypt` passed the JWE's initialization vector to `cipher.AEAD.Open` without checking its length. The Go standard library **panics** rather than returning an error when a GCM nonce is not exactly `NonceSize()` bytes, so a JWE carrying a wrong-sized IV crashes the decrypting goroutine.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T08:51:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T08:51:55", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/eclipse-keypont/gose/security/advisories/GHSA-265w-83cm-777q"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89318"], "assigner": "eclipse", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7a8dcc5e-5834-3ae2-848a-4042e8159b5b", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0.8.0 \u22640.13.0-rc1"}, {"id": "9129d577-cf74-34ef-ad1f-a6feff25aeb4", "product": {"name": "Eclipse KeyPont - GOSE", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.0.0-rc4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5e69266f-5ace-3e75-a4d4-a052848ebd95", "vendor": {"name": "Eclipse Foundation"}}], "isExploited": false}